.TH GH-CUSTOM-PROPERTIES 1 "16 September 2026" "gh-custom-properties 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gh-custom-properties \- view, add, edit, and delete GitHub custom repo properties
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gh-custom-properties [flags] [owner/repo | repo-url]
.B gh-custom-properties --file repos.txt [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
If no repo argument or --file is given, the TUI prompts for a repo to load.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -f, --file <path>
batch mode: file listing one repo (owner/repo or URL) per line
.TP
.B -t, --token <token>
GitHub token, overriding GITHUB_TOKEN / `gh auth token`
.TP
.B --backup-dir <path>
directory to write timestamped backups to (default $HOME/.gh-custom-properties/backups)
.TP
.B -h, -H, -?, --help, --HELP
show help
.TP
.B -v, --version
show version
.SH AUTHENTICATION
A GitHub token is required, resolved in this order:
  1. --token
  2. GITHUB_TOKEN environment variable
  3. `gh auth token` (if the gh CLI is installed and logged in)
.PP
The token needs permission to read and write custom properties on the
target repos, and to read the org's custom-property schema.
.SH REPO LIST FILE FORMAT (--FILE)
One repo per line, as "owner/repo" or a github.com URL. Blank lines and
lines starting with '#' are ignored.
.SH BACKUPS
Before any change is applied, a timestamped JSON snapshot of the prior
property values is written to the backup directory.
